p.src:
The entrepreneurial analogy is direct: $\text{first serious attempt}
\longrightarrow
\text{painful flop}
\longrightarrow
\begin{cases}
\text{stop},\\
\text{try again}.
\end{cases}$ Jones does not say the second branch is always superior. For many people, stopping is the right decision. Entrepreneurship is not for everyone. But some people discover that the first flop did not kill them, and that discovery changes the next decision.

