p.src:
Laura’s later success comes through reaching out. She has coffee with a real-estate executive and does not initially understand the scale of his network. When he says he wants the product for all his agents, the scale becomes concrete: $\text{one useful conversation}
\longrightarrow
11{,}000\ \text{possible users}.$ This is not a universal distribution formula. It is a local demonstration of why private reasoning is too small. Markets are discovered through people.

