p.src:
The most useful method is the hypothesis loop: $\text{hypothesis}
\rightarrow
\text{test}
\rightarrow
\text{evidence}
\rightarrow
\text{revised hypothesis}.$ Failure remains painful, but it need not become identity. To survive that loop, founders need community, advisors, health, sleep, family, and a motive that survives contact with reality. Entrepreneurship has rewards for certain people, but it is not for everyone. That is not an afterthought. It is one of the course’s central facts.

